cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this repository and the dated dataset snapshot used."
title: "MarketFlow: prediction-market microstructure measurements and an execution and risk-control system"
abstract: >-
  Measurements of prediction-market order flow — a zero-sum flow ledger over 439
  settled markets, event-contract fee geometry, repeated-size trading signatures and
  UMA settlement outcomes — together with the execution and risk-control system built
  on what the ledger shows: in that sample a modest aggregate selection edge was
  overwhelmed by modelled execution friction. The system covers event-level exposure
  and correlation accounting, capital-relative risk budgets and position sizing,
  market-quality and settlement gates, a delegated-mandate signing layer in which the
  account holder's own root controls the account and the service holds only side-bound
  agent credentials, and fail-loud monitoring. Raw trading tapes and wallet identities
  are not distributed.
type: software
authors:
  # CFF 1.2.0 definitions.entity: an organisation or project, identified by `name`
  # alone. Provenance for the earlier release is carried by the DOI in
  # `identifiers` rather than by a personal name.
